# 9/11/2026 -- Bumped layer sized down 50% after backtest strike-selection bug fix

## Why
The bumped backtest (bumped_spread_backtest.py) did not match prod strike selection.
Prod (bumped_spread_trader.py) always sells the parent's short strike one strike closer
to ATM. The legacy backtest both decremented the strike index AND lowered
min_strike_distance by $5. In the index-based strike logic the distance filter defines
index 0, so on days where spot sat within $1 of a strike (the parent's filter dropped the
near strike, ~20-25% of legs) the backtest landed TWO strikes closer than prod and
collected 2-3 dollars of credit prod never had. Found reconciling 9/9/26 (prod bumped
7635/7620 at 0.65, backtest 7640/7625 at 1.90). Confirmed in logs back to 7/16/26: 3 of
8 prod bumped triggers hit the condition (8/12, 8/13, 9/9).

Fixed 9/11/26. The backtest now uses prod semantics by default (--legacy-double-bump
reproduces the old method). Re-running history with the fix, 43 of 172 legs change and
the layer looks materially less attractive:

                     legacy PnL   fixed PnL   fixed worst day   fixed lifetime, no rebal veto
  IMBAL_GROWS         192,314     119,062       -96,444           ~62,000
  IMBAL_VS_MARKET     -18,065     -13,687       -26,169           -13,687
  IMBAL_SHRINKS       169,115      84,935       -32,045            84,935
  Combined            343,364     190,310

Without the retroactive rebal veto (which prod did not have before 9/9/26), the worst
single day for GROWS and VS_MARKET loses more than the strategy's lifetime PnL, and for
SHRINKS the worst day is ~38% of lifetime. On the affected days themselves the fix cuts
PnL from 272k to 119k (win rate 74% -> 95%, worst day -19.5k -> -2.1k): the legacy
method was booking near-ATM premium with tail risk prod never carried.

I still believe these are net positive, but with less conviction, so sizing is halved
rather than retired. Prod bumped history is short (first trade 4/22/26, 21 trades) and
already includes -60.9k (8/18, 1.9x oversized) and -33.9k (6/4) on GROWS.

