## Not changed / future option
- CLOSER tolerances and strike rules unchanged. The premium the legacy backtest was
  accidentally modeling (selling the strike nearest ATM on 1-lot days) is real and was
  profitable in the flawed backtest, but prod never traded it. If we want to capture it
  deliberately, the right vehicle is the CLOSER layer, not bumped: loosen the well_within
  thresholds in closer_strike_config.py (VS_MARKET: market_ratio 0.7 / imbal 1.5B;
  GROWS: imbal_340 < 1B / imbal_350 > 3B) and add an IMBAL_SHRINKS CLOSER variant. Would
  need its own backtest first. Not doing this now.
- Rebal veto, MAX_ATM_VOL 0.14, BUMP_STEP, SPREAD_WIDTH unchanged.
